course: dictionary
lesson: 15864
title: Unfrozen: no longer frozen
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word unfrozen is made of two parts: un- and frozen. The prefix un- often means not, or the opposite of, so unfrozen means no longer frozen.
explain: «The frozen peas were unfrozen after an hour on the kitchen table.» The peas are no longer hard and icy. The warm kitchen is a clue that they have thawed out.
explain: The word can also be used in other places. «The bank unfroze Sam's account, so he could spend his money again.» Here unfrozen means blocked money can be used again. Always check your meaning by putting it back into the sentence.
fact: The prefix un- often means not or the opposite of, as in unhappy, unfair and unfrozen.
fact: Unfrozen means no longer frozen. It can mean thawed, like melted ice, or never frozen at all.
fact: «Unfrozen» can describe money or accounts that were blocked and can now be used again.
fact: «Unfrozen» can describe a computer screen or app that stopped responding and now works again.
fact: Frozen meat must be fully unfrozen, or defrosted, before you cook it, so it cooks evenly and safely.
exercise: «The ice cubes were unfrozen after an hour in the warm kitchen.» What does unfrozen mean? | *No longer frozen; melted | Very cold and hard | Stuck in the freezer again | Covered in snow
exercise: The bank unfroze Sam's account. What can Sam do now? | Hide the money under his bed | *Spend his money again | Freeze his money even harder | Lose all of his money
exercise: My game screen stopped working, but now it is unfrozen. What does that tell you? | It is frozen solid | *It works again after it stopped responding | It has been switched off for good | It is covered in ice
test: What does the prefix un- mean in unfrozen? | Under the ice | *Not, or the opposite of | Very cold | Again and again
test: Frozen meat must be fully ___ before you cook it. | Wrapped | *unfrozen | Salted | Burnt
exam: Mia's account was ___ by the bank, so she could use her money again. | empty | frozen | *unfrozen | sealed
